  "purpose": "Nexus session/factory integration preserving the original business workspace, templates and standalone account source. Includes six-factory isolation, retirement of legacy accounts, canonical audit identity, complete blob version forwarding, combined product/material authorization, request-body reauthentication, locked session boundaries, guarded navigation, read-only shipment viewing, and export ownership checks. Acceptance fixes preserve customs business dates, defined names, print scopes, cached totals, hidden sheet states and outbound stock calculations; repair generated workbook XML order and empty merges; retain template print metadata with complete-width auxiliary forms; and support narrow-screen editors, tables and purchase-contract printing. Upstream VM test fixtures include the new read-only state. Nexus raw database administration is retired at menu, route, session and both API boundaries; historical grants remain inactive without deleting business data or the preserved standalone source. Business navigation groups the existing URLs into two collapsible sections with unchanged leaf permissions and supplier quote labeling. Embedded layout removes the duplicate header and bridges material alerts/mobile navigation to the host with connection-bound message checks.",
